 \subsection{Significance of result}
-\humanauthor[P2-12 r6]{Matched-exposure verification shows that the quality ranking depends on the contract, while the efficiency gains hold under every contract we tested. At no pre-registered token budget is GPT A22 better per token, so its fixed-time standing reflects its extra exposure, not better learning. Opus pushed the same lever further: its recipes were worse still per token, and most of its decode gain came from graph replay whose recording the metric did not time. A benchmark that ranks agents under a time budget therefore partly ranks how fast their candidates train. Quality gains should be rechecked at controlled exposure, and speed gains with end-to-end timing.}
